# Copy to signing.local.mk (gitignored) for stable code signing so macOS permission
# grants (mic/screen/accessibility) persist across rebuilds. Find your identity with:
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# Then set the SHA-1 below (and your team id):
# SIGN_FLAGS = CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=<your-sha1> DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=<your-team>
#
# Why this matters: macOS (TCC) keys a permission grant by bundle id *plus* the binary's
# code-signing requirement. Without a stable identity, Xcode signs ad-hoc and the requirement
# is pinned to the binary's cdhash — which changes on every build, so every rebuild is a new
# app to macOS and you re-grant Screen Recording each time.
#
# An "Apple Development" certificate gives a stable requirement, but note it expires in about a
# year; when it renews, the requirement changes and dev grants reset once. A "Developer ID
# Application" certificate lasts ~5 years if you prefer fewer resets.
#
# This does NOT collide with the released app: Debug builds use bundle id
# com.tomwu.ListenToMe.dev ("ListenToMe (Dev)") while the release dmg uses
# com.tomwu.ListenToMe, so the two hold independent grants. See project.yml and
# docs/RELEASING.md.
